{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>אגור</b> [agr]. I wonder whether it is from the root of ויגר מואב (Genesis 19:37). The translator [Targum] says it is from the root אגרה in the sense of harvest. The correct interpretation is that it is from the root of תגרה. The verse speaks in the manner of men, for the understanding of the hearers." "<b>ינכרו.</b> The opposite of יכירו, like ויתנכר אליהם." "<b>פעל כל זאת.</b> Concerning the tribes."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {0 "Resolved המתרגם as 'the translator,' i.e., Onkelos; his rendering of אגור connects it to אגר/קציר (hire/harvest). Ibn Ezra's suggested alternative, תגרה, denotes stir up / provoke."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:26:07.768263789Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}